“Until now, these feelings of inferiority and differentiation were the real things that gave me the strength and the power to succeed.”
He wanted to prove that he was "someone", he said not to disappoint anyone who could possibly find out what it is with his sexuality.
The two-time bronze-grade bronze medal has become a high-profile LGBT rights campaigner and took advantage of his presence at this year's Commonwealth Games in Australia to appeal more countries to decriminalize homosexuality.
